msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:53
msgid "Organization name"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:55
msgid "Leave empty to use the site title."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:62
msgid "Address"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:63
msgid "Printed under the name. One line per line."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:69
msgid "Logo"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:70
msgid "Printed above the organization name. Kept small on purpose — this is correspondence, not a flyer. Email programs often refuse to load images, so the name is always printed as text underneath and the letter reads correctly without it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:76
msgid "Contact for questions"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:78
msgid "Where a court or school should direct questions about a letter. This is the number somebody phones to check a reference code, so make it one that is answered."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:87
msgid "Signed by"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:88
msgid "Printed under the signature line. Left empty, the line prints unlabelled — which looks unfinished, and is meant to."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:94
msgid "Their title"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:95
msgid "Printed under the name — \"Volunteer Coordinator\", \"Executive Director\". It tells a reader what standing the person signing has to say what the letter says."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:105
msgid "Opening paragraph"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:107
msgid "Leave empty to use the wording shown. Plain text only — bold and italic survive, other markup does not."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:115
msgid "Disclaimer"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:117
msgid "Your counsel may want particular wording, so this is yours to change. It cannot be emptied: saving it blank restores the default. A letter with no disclaimer is a letter that has quietly started implying this plugin certified something."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:125
msgid "What the reference code proves"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:127
msgid "Also cannot be emptied. Without it, a reader reasonably assumes a code means some outside body issued the document."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:137
msgid "List every shift"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:138
msgid "On by default. A total with nothing behind it is a number the reader has to take on faith, which is what this document exists to avoid."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:144
msgid "Also list hours nobody has verified"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:145
msgid "Off by default. When on, unverified shifts appear marked as such and are still excluded from the verified total — they are never quietly added in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:151
msgid "Reference prefix"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:152
msgid "Prepended to every reference code. Letters and numbers only — the code gets read aloud over the phone and typed back in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:161
msgid "Subject line"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:162
#: inc/emails.php:117
msgid "Your volunteer service verification from {org}"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:170
msgid "Covering note"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:171
msgid "Appears above the letter in the email, outside it. The letter itself is identical whether printed or emailed, and this is how a short “here is your letter” message gets added without changing the document."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:178
msgid "From name"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:179
msgid "Leave both empty to use whatever WordPress would have used."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:185
msgid "From address"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:186
msgid "Use an address at your own domain. A letter sent from an address somewhere else is the thing a spam filter is most likely to hold back, and the volunteer never learns it was sent."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:195
msgid "Round hours to"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:197
msgid "Do not round"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:198
msgid "5 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:199
msgid "10 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:200
msgid "15 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:201
msgid "30 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:202
msgid "A whole hour"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:204
msgid "Always to the nearest, never up — rounding up is the organization crediting hours nobody worked."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:210
msgid "Show hours as"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:212
msgid "Decimal is what a court order is usually written in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:218
msgid "Allow shifts dated in the future"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:219
msgid "Off by default. A shift dated next Tuesday is a typo far more often than a plan, and on a document a court reads it discredits the whole record."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:225
msgid "Let volunteers send in their own hours"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:226
msgid "Off until you switch it on. With it on, this site accepts a name, an email address and a date from anonymous visitors — everything they send arrives unverified and waits for a staff member. Nothing they enter appears publicly."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:232
msgid "The page the form is on"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:233
msgid "Add the Volunteer Hours Form block, or the [volunteer_hours_form] shortcode, to a page and choose it here. Submissions are only accepted on this page, and it is pinned by ID so renaming it changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:239
#: inc/admin-settings.php:316
msgid "Require a code"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:240
msgid "Optional. A word you give people at the front desk, which the form then asks for. Not a security control — it is the difference between a form the whole internet can post to and one only people who have been handed a card will bother with."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:246
msgid "Keep volunteer records for"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:248
msgid "\"Keep indefinitely\" is a legitimate answer, and it is the default — a plugin that deleted records on a schedule it chose would eventually destroy the six weeks of Saturdays somebody needs for a court date. What is not legitimate is never deciding, which is why this tab nags until you save it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:254
msgid "When a record is old enough"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:256
msgid "Remove the name and contact details, keep the hours"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:257
msgid "Delete the record and its shifts entirely"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:259
msgid "Anonymising is usually right: your grant reporting and your Form 990 need the hours, and the hours identify nobody once the name is gone."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:265
msgid "Measured from"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:267
msgid "Their last recorded shift"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:268
msgid "The last time a shift of theirs was verified"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:270
msgid "The clock runs on the whole person, not on each shift — a record is removed when the person has been inactive this long, and their old shifts go with them. Measuring from the last shift is what most policies mean. Measuring from the last verification is later, sometimes much later, because a shift written up in March and attested in June counts from June."
msgstr ""

